 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "Correctness",
   "items": [
    "Two customers racing for one car: the booking_day primary key lets exactly one win",
    "Same Idempotency-Key replayed: the original payment comes back, no second charge",
    "The payment row exists before the (mock, in-process) gateway is called"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "When confirm fails",
   "items": [
    "Booking unconfirmable: payment compensates (refund) and cancels the booking",
    "Timeout: the reconciliation sweeper retries confirm later; confirm is idempotent",
    "Notification is off the request path: an outage cannot fail a booking"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Why this use case",
   "items": [
    "It exercises local JWT, a cross-service read, the snapshot, DB-enforced concurrency, the saga, idempotency and the outbox",
    "No DB connection is held across an HTTP call: the fix that took load from under 50 to over 400 actions/s"
   ]
  }
 ]
